dogscoff@eudoramail.com wrote:
> M.O. wrote:

> Also, every uranium item in you main inventory adds one point to your
> "radiation" counter per turn. When that counter hits 1000, choose
> randomly from the following outcomes (Weighted so that the ones at the
> end of the list are more common).

"Every uranium item" meaning every uranium wand.

I think this is too predictable. It would be better to give it just a
1/1000 chance every turn. This is the usual way in NetHack, and in the
long run, this would mean that it still happens the same number of
times, on averate.

I think weighing should also take your constitution into account: the
higher it is, the lower on the below list you'd end up:

   max ( 11 , min( 1 , round(sqrt(rnd(143))) + rnd(Con) ) )

or something like that...

> 1 - "You mutate! You grow wings!" Get flying intrinsic until you next
> polymorph.

Or until (3) happens.

> 2 - "You mutate! You feel a change coming over you!" Polymorph.
> 3 - "You mutate! Your [limb] becomes unusable!" If winged, lose flying
> intrinsic. Otherwise, leg damage.

Leg damage does not imply it has become unusable. It just decreases your
carrying capacity.

> 4 - "You feel deathly sick". Made ill as per pestilence attack etc.

Good thing that this has only a small chance of happening. You might
want to put it on 1.

> 5 - "Your body mutates massively. Your [armour] splits apart" 1
> randomly chosen piece of worn armour destroyed. 1d6-4 (ie between -3
> and 3) added to either str, dex or con.

Difficult to keep track of. You'd have to, since you wouldn't be able to
wear armour afterwards (also, no cloaks or shirts). And this would have
to be kept track of for feet, head and hands as well.

Note that 1d6-4 is not between -3 and 3, but between -3 and 2. For the
real nitpicks, it is *between* -4 and 3 ("between" not including the
marginal numbers).

> 6 - "You feel light-headed" Character glows in the dark (@ acts as
> permanent light source).

I like the pun, but this might be too powerful (unless it also wakes up
or attracks monsters and has a radius of only two, like Sunsword).

> 7 - "You hair|fur falls out" lose CH points - (bald ppl aren't
> necessarily unnattractive imo, but anyway...)

Temporary or also permanent?

> 8 - "Your teeth fall out" lose CH points and any bite attack you may
> have had. Unable to eat anything except tins of soup.

Taking away attack types might require major changes to the source, but
I really don't know for sure.

> 9 - "Your fingernails/ claws fall out" lose 1 CH, lose 1 dex, lose any
> claw attacks you may have had.

Again, temporary or permanent?

> 10 - "You feel very unwell." Lose 3d6 hit points, abuse constitution.

I don't think "unwell" is proper English... Would the con loss be
permanent (ie affect your maximum constitution)?

> 11 - "You feel sick". As if poisoned.

Reasonable for the most often occurring one.

> All the above effects (except #2, and including the positive ones) can
> be remedied with prayer/ unihorn/ !oRA, /"cure sickness", as
> appropriate.

Note that the "deathly sick" effect has to be cures almost immediately,
and a unicorn horn isn't reliable, even when blessed. If the message
appears while you're walking through a corridor without anything
dangerous in sight, it may easily be missed, since you (obviously)
wouldn't have your guard up.

I think this would be too harsh, and cause of a number of annoying
deaths.

> Some way of linking these effects to their cause would be necessary
> for unspoiled players. Perhaps uranium objects could "feel
> dangerously warm to the touch" when picked up or used, or something
> like hat. Oh, and some suitably cryptic fortunes entries.

That would be necessary indeed, I think.

